eference/websocket/markets#webpage\"},\"dateModified\":\"2026-05-31T00:31:12.643Z\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://docs.polymarket.us/#organization\"},\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://docs.polymarket.us#website\"}}]}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"51:Tce7,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"/*\r\n * Custom styling for the Polymarket US documentation.\r\n *\r\n * Mintlify automatically loads any `.css` file in the project root and applies\r\n * it on every page. See:\r\n * https://www.mintlify.com/docs/customize/custom-scripts#add-custom-css\r\n *\r\n * NOTE: Mintlify's exposed selectors / theme utility classes are subject to\r\n * change between major theme versions — re-verify these rules with\r\n * inspect-element after a `mint` upgrade.\r\n */\r\n\r\n/*\r\n * Variable-width (content-sized) table columns.\r\n *\r\n * The mint theme renders every markdown table with a Tailwind utility that\r\n * forces a minimum width on each data cell (effectively `[\u0026_td]:min-w-[150px]`).\r\n * On dense tables this makes narrow columns (a sequence number, a short\r\n * currency value) occupy the same ~150px as long prose columns, so every\r\n * column looks roughly equal-width regardless of its content.\r\n *\r\n * Relaxing the per-cell minimum lets the browser's default `table-layout: auto`\r\n * size each column to its content while the table still fills the available\r\n * width (`w-full` is left intact). Short columns shrink; prose columns grow.\r\n *\r\n * Scoped to `#content-container` so it only affects rendered doc content.\r\n */\r\n#content-container table {\r\n  table-layout: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n#content-container table th,\r\n#content-container table td {\r\n  min-width: 0 !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/*\r\n * Keep cells that hold a single numeric / currency value on one line so the\r\n * running-balance columns stay compact and readable.\r\n */\r\n#content-container table td[data-numeric=\"true\"] {\r\n  white-space: nowrap;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/*\r\n * Keep code tokens in table cells on one line.\r\n *\r\n * Identifier-style cells (`participant_account_id`, `cash_order_qty`,\r\n * `MoneyAmount`, …) in the Field / Type / Component columns of API tables\r\n * were being broken mid-token at underscores by the theme's overflow-wrap,\r\n * squeezing those columns and making them hard to scan. Code tokens are\r\n * atomic — never wrap inside them; prose (Description) columns still wrap\r\n * normally between tokens.\r\n */\r\n#content-container table td code,\r\n#content-container table th code {\r\n  white-space: nowrap;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/*\r\n * Rewards CTA — the \"View polymarket.us/rewards\" card on\r\n * /incentives/liquidity, wrapped in `\u003cdiv className=\"rewards-cta\"\u003e`.\r\n *\r\n * Renders that one card as a solid brand-blue button (docs.json\r\n * colors.primary) so the link out to the live rewards page is\r\n * unmissable — deliberately the only blue surface on the page.\r\n *\r\n * Selectors follow the card's rendered DOM (`.card` +\r\n * `data-component-part` hooks). Icons render as mask-image SVGs whose\r\n * `background-color` is the visible fill, hence the icon rule below.\r\n */\r\n.rewards-cta .card {\r\n  background: #165dfc !important;\r\n  border-color: transparent !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.rewards-cta .card:hover {\r\n  background: #1253e0 !important;\r\n  border-color: transparent !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.rewards-cta .card [data-component-part=\"card-title\"] {\r\n  color: #fff !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.rewards-cta .card [data-component-part=\"card-content\"] {\r\n  color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.85) !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.rewards-cta .card [data-component-part=\"card-icon\"] svg {\r\n  background-color: #fff !important;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.rewards-cta .card #card-link-arrow-icon {\r\n  color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.8) !important;\r\n}\r\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4b:[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"pageMetadata\":\"$19:props:children:props:pageMetadata\",\"mdxExtracts\":\"$19:props:children:props:childre